  "body": "Create a hardware air-cut tester kit under `docs/tester-kits/haas-ngc-3axis/` and a verification test under `crates/app/tests/`.\n\nFollow the existing MicroArc kit layout in `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/README.md` and `crates/app/tests/microarc_test_part.rs`. Build this kit after the Slice 1 Haas `.mch` files and `haas.cps` NGC safety fixes merge (`#1976`, `#1977`):\n- Include a `.camproj` test project that uses a Haas 3-axis machine definition (such as `haas-vf2.mch`).\n- Include operations covering face/contour with `G187` smoothing, `G2`/`G3` arcs, `G81`/`G82`/`G83` drilling, `G84` rigid tapping, and probing if equipped.\n- Write clear air-cut setup instructions (`README.md`) telling operators to run with Z zero shifted safely above the table and dry-run at low rapid override first.\n- Add a golden `.nc` file and a Rust integration test in `crates/app/tests/` that loads the `.camproj`, builds toolpaths, posts with `haas.cps`, and asserts zero errors or warnings.\n\nDone means: `docs/tester-kits/haas-ngc-3axis/` holds the `.camproj`, `README.md`, and golden `.nc`, and the new test in `crates/app/tests/` passes.\n\nPart of #1961\n",
